 Strong Passwords and Password Managers
Weak passwords are one of the most common vulnerabilities in personal cybersecurity.
Learning internet usage includes understanding how to create strong, unique passwords for each account and using a password manager to store them securely.
A good password is long, complex, and not reused across sites. Password managers generate and remember these credentials, so users only need to remember one master password. 
This practice significantly reduces the risk of account takeover and identity theft, 
which are often the result of credential stuffing attacks.
